      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "Instructor: So that's it for the HTTP module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "Quite a long module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "where you learned a lot about the angle or HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "Now the most common task you will do is of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 16.77,
          "en": "that you send requests by using post, get, and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.77,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "by adding a URL, possibly a request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 22.02,
          "en": "and maybe some request headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.02,
          "end": 23.94,
          "en": "This will be your bread and butter thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "and therefore this is the task you should practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "and you should feel confident about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 33.06,
          "en": "Always remember that these methods like get and post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.06,
          "end": 36,
          "en": "give you back an observable to which you have to subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "to actually kick off the request and to send it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 42.51,
          "en": "Since it is an observable, you can use operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.51,
          "end": 46.74,
          "en": "RXJS operators, to transform the data, log data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "catch errors, or whatever you want to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 51.99,
          "en": "but ultimately, you need to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.99,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "And you can do this in a service or in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "depending on where you need to work with the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 60.78,
          "en": "And in the subscribe method, you pass in a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "to handle the data you get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 66.273,
          "en": "and possibly also an error handling function, like this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "This is how you generally work with HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 72.39,
          "en": "Now you've got advanced features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.39,
          "end": 76.35,
          "en": "like the possibility of setting what you wanna observe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.35,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "if you are interested in the,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "or just the body of the response, or all the events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "which type of data should be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "You can set query perms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "and you have the very useful features of inter setters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.45,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "which can really help you save time and code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 99.33,
          "en": "if you have some header that needs to be appended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.33,
          "end": 101.85,
          "en": "to every outgoing request, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.85,
          "end": 103.47,
          "en": "And as I already mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.47,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "we'll see inter setters in action again later in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "once we add authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 109.86,
          "en": "For now, this is it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.86,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "Let's now move on to the Chorus Project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 115.443,
          "en": "and practice using these HTTP requests there.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
